  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nNortheast flow coming off of Lake Erie has increased low level\nmoisture enough for fog to develop. This has spread into parts of\nwest central Ohio and some areas in central Ohio north of Columbus.\nThe lowest visibilities are forecast to remain across west central\nOhio, so a dense fog advisory has been issued for that area. The fog\nshould diminish by mid morning. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nMid level ridge extending from the western Gulf to the western Great\nLakes will shift slightly eastward into the early part of the week. \nSurface high situated east of the area will remain through the \nweekend. Then a weak front will sag south across the area Monday into\nMonday night. \n\nThe mid level ridge gets slowly suppressed, finally breaking down by\nmid week as a short wave lifts out of the southern Plains and up the\nOhio Valley. The front will wash out as another high moves from\nOntario to the northeast Atlantic coast. \n\nAll put together, the extended period of dry conditions will persist\nwell into next week, perhaps the entirety of the week. Temperatures\nwill be above normal.",
